1
00:00:38,539 --> 00:00:41,959
MY BIAS, MY BOSS

2
00:00:50,592 --> 00:00:53,345
There's quite a competition
to launch their brand with us.

3
00:00:53,637 --> 00:00:55,388
There are over 30 brands

4
00:00:55,389 --> 00:00:57,015
that have sent us samples
just this week.

5
00:00:57,599 --> 00:01:00,644
Many of these are dupes of what I saw
at the last Paris Fashion Week.

6
00:01:01,019 --> 00:01:03,354
It had many innovative designs

7
00:01:03,355 --> 00:01:05,731
so it looks like domestic brands
were heavily influenced.

8
00:01:05,732 --> 00:01:08,067
If all they can do is copy

9
00:01:08,068 --> 00:01:09,778
they can't work with Appello.

10
00:01:10,904 --> 00:01:12,239
I'll look into just this brand.

11
00:01:12,990 --> 00:01:15,658
All right.
Ms. Seo, please help out with that.

12
00:01:15,659 --> 00:01:17,827
I'll join you right away
after figuring out the display.

13
00:01:17,828 --> 00:01:20,997
Yes, I'll get the models ready
for the fitting.

14
00:01:20,998 --> 00:01:22,541
- Okay, tell me when they're ready.
- Yes, sir.

15
00:01:25,877 --> 00:01:26,920
This is just like you.

16
00:01:27,713 --> 00:01:29,464
They aren't generic

17
00:01:30,716 --> 00:01:32,466
and they carry their own identity.

18
00:01:32,467 --> 00:01:34,302
That's how Appello started.

19
00:01:34,303 --> 00:01:36,345
I was just collecting the clothes
I wanted to wear

20
00:01:36,346 --> 00:01:37,806
which turned
into a tiny curated boutique.

21
00:01:38,599 --> 00:01:41,393
And now, it's a platform
that carries hundreds of brands.

22
00:01:42,019 --> 00:01:43,562
The pressure is different now.

23
00:01:44,104 --> 00:01:46,188
Which you're carrying very well.

24
00:01:46,189 --> 00:01:47,232
I'm in charge of the direction.

25
00:01:47,649 --> 00:01:50,444
And if that direction is too skewed,
everyone who's following will fall.

26
00:01:50,736 --> 00:01:52,445
Gosh, I know

27
00:01:52,446 --> 00:01:53,947
that this is the time
to be more inclusive.

28
00:01:58,035 --> 00:01:59,119
Yes, sir.

29
00:02:00,412 --> 00:02:03,707
Yes, Mr. Kang. I'll do as you say
and pick up more mainstream designs.

30
00:02:08,295 --> 00:02:10,380
EPISODE 2

31
00:02:12,758 --> 00:02:14,091
Okay.

32
00:02:14,092 --> 00:02:16,302
That bracelet on the man's hand.

33
00:02:16,303 --> 00:02:17,512
- Take note of it.
- Yes.

34
00:02:20,265 --> 00:02:23,142
Please get a tie
that's as bright as this one.

35
00:02:23,143 --> 00:02:24,645
Right. Yes, sir.

36
00:02:25,687 --> 00:02:26,772
Great work, everyone.

37
00:02:27,397 --> 00:02:28,522
- Yes.
- Goodbye.

38
00:02:28,523 --> 00:02:30,232
Text me the pictures we took today.

39
00:02:30,233 --> 00:02:33,487
- Okay. Goodbye, Mr. Lee.
- Okay.

40
00:02:55,384 --> 00:02:58,679
D.N.X! D.N.X! We love you, D.N.X!

41
00:03:18,657 --> 00:03:20,909
You dropped this.

42
00:03:29,626 --> 00:03:31,545
Right. Thank you.

43
00:03:36,383 --> 00:03:37,384
Getting in?

44
00:03:38,635 --> 00:03:39,636
What?

45
00:03:41,346 --> 00:03:43,515
Oh, I am.

46
00:03:59,656 --> 00:04:01,031
Don't be so nervous, Da-reum.

47
00:04:01,032 --> 00:04:03,160
Try to act as naturally as possible.

48
00:04:10,083 --> 00:04:11,209
NAM DA-REUM

49
00:04:12,419 --> 00:04:14,171
- You must be one of the new hires.
- Sorry?

50
00:04:19,217 --> 00:04:20,218
Yes.

51
00:04:20,802 --> 00:04:22,095
Why weren't you there
at the welcome dinner?

52
00:04:25,557 --> 00:04:27,768
I got a bit drunk last night

53
00:04:28,602 --> 00:04:29,895
and went home early.

54
00:04:30,937 --> 00:04:32,731
I see.

55
00:04:34,858 --> 00:04:36,818
Anyway, it's nice to meet you,
Da-reum.

56
00:04:41,406 --> 00:04:42,866
How do you know my name?

57
00:04:44,618 --> 00:04:45,786
I look forward to working with you.

58
00:05:00,133 --> 00:05:01,551
I'll do my best.

59
00:05:05,138 --> 00:05:06,139
See you around.

60
00:05:08,183 --> 00:05:09,518
Yes, Mr. Lee.

61
00:05:16,691 --> 00:05:17,901
Goodbye.

62
00:05:39,047 --> 00:05:40,215
My gosh.

63
00:05:41,550 --> 00:05:43,300
My gosh!

64
00:05:43,301 --> 00:05:46,972
I shook hands with Chan!

65
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:50,809
My gosh!

66
00:05:53,687 --> 00:05:56,021
Great job on not getting too nervous.

67
00:05:56,022 --> 00:05:57,566
Good one, Da-reum.

68
00:06:11,788 --> 00:06:12,956
Goodbye.

69
00:06:20,964 --> 00:06:25,260
WOLHWA SILVER WORKSHOP

70
00:06:37,814 --> 00:06:41,401
Hey, what have you been
doing here for days?

71
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:44,070
Are you looking for a career change?

72
00:06:44,362 --> 00:06:45,530
Should I do that?

73
00:06:47,073 --> 00:06:48,741
D.N.X has disbanded

74
00:06:48,742 --> 00:06:50,744
and not many would remember Lee Chan.

75
00:06:52,412 --> 00:06:53,413
Hey.

76
00:06:53,955 --> 00:06:55,040
I'm pretty good, aren't I?

77
00:06:55,874 --> 00:06:58,376
You might as well
open a jewelry studio.

78
00:07:01,588 --> 00:07:04,882
Hey, clean up everything
before I come back.

79
00:07:04,883 --> 00:07:05,884
Okay?

80
00:07:06,384 --> 00:07:07,510
Okay?

81
00:07:34,329 --> 00:07:36,455
- Hello.
- Hello.

82
00:07:36,456 --> 00:07:38,500
By any chance, how much is this?

83
00:07:38,959 --> 00:07:42,544
This is a DIY jewelry studio,
so we do not sell any items.

84
00:07:42,545 --> 00:07:45,006
This was
one of our customers' designs.

85
00:07:45,340 --> 00:07:49,593
This is the exact shape
that my all-time favorite celebrity

86
00:07:49,594 --> 00:07:51,596
always draws
when he signs autographs.

87
00:07:52,472 --> 00:07:54,056
Today's my birthday

88
00:07:54,057 --> 00:07:56,350
so I want to buy it for myself
as a gift.

89
00:07:56,351 --> 00:07:57,811
Can I please buy it?

90
00:07:58,853 --> 00:08:00,354
I'm sorry.

91
00:08:00,355 --> 00:08:02,649
But why don't you
try making it yourself?

92
00:08:04,442 --> 00:08:07,528
I don't think
I can make it look exactly the same.

93
00:08:07,529 --> 00:08:11,282
It's not as difficult as you think.

94
00:08:13,576 --> 00:08:14,828
It's okay.

95
00:08:15,578 --> 00:08:17,955
I understand. Thank you.

96
00:08:17,956 --> 00:08:19,665
- Sure.
- Goodbye.

97
00:08:19,666 --> 00:08:20,875
Okay. Goodbye.

98
00:08:24,129 --> 00:08:27,257
WOLHWA SILVER WORKSHOP

99
00:08:44,065 --> 00:08:45,400
It was you from back then.

100
00:08:50,113 --> 00:08:52,949
- Great work today.
- Goodbye!

101
00:08:53,908 --> 00:08:57,245
We've all done so well today!
See you tomorrow.

102
00:08:57,620 --> 00:09:00,331
See you tomorrow! Bye!

103
00:09:01,791 --> 00:09:05,961
It looks like something great
must've happened to Da-reum.

104
00:09:05,962 --> 00:09:08,757
Right? Our team has been
swamped with work lately.

105
00:09:09,090 --> 00:09:12,259
Min-a, if it's okay with you

106
00:09:12,260 --> 00:09:14,053
why don't we grab a glass of beer?

107
00:09:14,054 --> 00:09:16,097
Gosh, beer?

108
00:09:17,015 --> 00:09:18,099
No.

109
00:09:20,143 --> 00:09:21,186
No?

110
00:09:27,776 --> 00:09:29,277
You must be one of the new hires.

111
00:09:36,367 --> 00:09:37,535
SUNGJU STATION

112
00:09:41,414 --> 00:09:42,582
It's nice to meet you, Da-reum.

113
00:09:44,501 --> 00:09:47,462
It was so great to meet you.

114
00:09:53,051 --> 00:09:54,302
See you around.

115
00:10:07,357 --> 00:10:09,191
See you!

116
00:10:09,192 --> 00:10:11,610
Chan, let us meet again!

117
00:10:11,611 --> 00:10:13,029
See you, Da-reum!

118
00:10:14,405 --> 00:10:15,532
Bye!

119
00:10:20,245 --> 00:10:21,496
Are you that happy?

120
00:10:23,039 --> 00:10:24,040
Yes.

121
00:10:24,582 --> 00:10:26,834
Someone might think
you just won the lottery.

122
00:10:26,835 --> 00:10:28,544
It's her ultimate fan moment.

123
00:10:28,545 --> 00:10:31,255
Fans who lived outside Seoul
can't go to music show recordings.

124
00:10:31,256 --> 00:10:35,844
And at concerts, they look this small
so you can't even see their faces.

125
00:10:36,386 --> 00:10:38,887
You've made it, Namda.

126
00:10:38,888 --> 00:10:41,765
So? Would you like to smell my hand?

127
00:10:41,766 --> 00:10:43,350
Jeez.

128
00:10:43,351 --> 00:10:45,102
- No!
- Me too!

129
00:10:45,103 --> 00:10:48,106
No, it's going to wear off.
I can't lose it!

130
00:10:50,525 --> 00:10:52,861
Today is the first time
I've seen Chan in person.

131
00:10:53,987 --> 00:10:56,655
I'll always celebrate this day.

132
00:10:56,656 --> 00:10:59,409
You've always insisted
Chan gave you that necklace.

133
00:10:59,742 --> 00:11:01,661
Do you finally admit
that you were overly hopeful?

134
00:11:07,375 --> 00:11:11,963
But no one else
could have possibly made this.

135
00:11:24,017 --> 00:11:25,143
Excuse me.

136
00:11:30,315 --> 00:11:31,316
Happy birthday.

137
00:12:05,975 --> 00:12:08,977
He definitely sounded like him too.

138
00:12:08,978 --> 00:12:12,023
You're just misremembering
as a hopeful fan.

139
00:12:13,650 --> 00:12:14,817
You think so?

140
00:12:15,068 --> 00:12:16,318
Well, anyway.

141
00:12:16,319 --> 00:12:20,155
I finally met him in person. My gosh!

142
00:12:20,156 --> 00:12:21,824
I'm not dreaming, am I?

143
00:12:23,743 --> 00:12:25,202
It hurts!

144
00:12:25,203 --> 00:12:26,328
- It's not.
- It hurts.

145
00:12:26,329 --> 00:12:28,039
APPELLO

146
00:12:30,208 --> 00:12:32,292
This time, the overseas training
for outstanding employees

147
00:12:32,293 --> 00:12:34,212
will be held
at the New York Fashion Week.

148
00:12:34,587 --> 00:12:35,588
New York?

149
00:12:35,964 --> 00:12:37,215
It sounds perfect.

150
00:12:37,632 --> 00:12:39,175
You'll get to see a lot

151
00:12:40,426 --> 00:12:42,637
and also have a mountain of work.

152
00:12:43,179 --> 00:12:45,598
Overseas training
for outstanding employees?

153
00:12:46,099 --> 00:12:48,517
It's a tradition of sorts
that Director Lee has made

154
00:12:48,518 --> 00:12:51,019
since the foundation of Appello.

155
00:12:51,020 --> 00:12:52,813
Once a year,
we pick out an outstanding employee

156
00:12:52,814 --> 00:12:54,190
to do a project abroad.

157
00:12:54,857 --> 00:12:57,652
Someone will be chosen
early next year.

158
00:12:59,070 --> 00:13:01,114
Thank you. Come here, Min-a.

159
00:13:02,115 --> 00:13:03,449
Does that mean

160
00:13:03,825 --> 00:13:05,826
Director Lee will go on the trip too?

161
00:13:05,827 --> 00:13:06,911
Of course.

162
00:13:07,370 --> 00:13:09,746
He has never missed it once.

163
00:13:09,747 --> 00:13:11,707
Who picks out
the outstanding employee?

164
00:13:11,708 --> 00:13:12,709
Mr. Kang.

165
00:13:15,795 --> 00:13:17,088
Mr. Kang?

166
00:13:28,808 --> 00:13:30,059
AVOID MR. KANG

167
00:13:30,476 --> 00:13:31,477
WORK HARD!

168
00:13:35,648 --> 00:13:37,483
EMPLOYEE OVERSEAS TRAINING!
GET ON MR. KANG'S GOOD SIDE!

169
00:13:41,112 --> 00:13:42,238
Well...

170
00:13:43,031 --> 00:13:46,784
Is it okay
for my goal to change so drastically?

171
00:13:47,952 --> 00:13:50,163
No, Da-reum.

172
00:13:50,705 --> 00:13:52,457
You can do this.

173
00:13:55,126 --> 00:13:56,210
First of all

174
00:13:57,545 --> 00:14:01,215
I must figure out
what Mr. Kang is like.

175
00:14:04,927 --> 00:14:07,180
Ms. Kim, this is for you.

176
00:14:10,099 --> 00:14:11,809
Ms. Kim.

177
00:14:12,143 --> 00:14:14,771
So what does Mr. Kang like?

178
00:14:15,521 --> 00:14:16,564
Why are you asking about him?

179
00:14:18,566 --> 00:14:22,570
I wasn't exactly
on my best behavior since day one

180
00:14:23,112 --> 00:14:24,821
so I wanted to improve my reputation

181
00:14:24,822 --> 00:14:26,616
and do my best at work.

182
00:14:27,658 --> 00:14:28,701
Is that so?

183
00:14:29,243 --> 00:14:30,787
Mr. Kang...

184
00:14:32,830 --> 00:14:36,209
He only uses the brown capsules
for the coffee machine.

185
00:14:39,754 --> 00:14:40,880
The brown ones?

186
00:14:41,839 --> 00:14:43,131
Chocolate latte.

187
00:14:43,132 --> 00:14:44,967
He has a sweet tooth,
unlike how he seems.

188
00:14:46,010 --> 00:14:47,762
GUIDE TO WINNING CEO KANG HA-GI
OFFER HIM CHOCOLATE LATTE

189
00:14:54,894 --> 00:14:56,603
Mr. Kang.

190
00:14:56,604 --> 00:14:58,980
Would you like
a cup of sweet chocolate latte?

191
00:14:58,981 --> 00:15:00,149
I made it just now.

192
00:15:03,528 --> 00:15:06,405
No, I only drink one cup a day
because of my blood glucose level.

193
00:15:06,406 --> 00:15:08,491
I've already had it,
so enjoy it for yourself.

194
00:15:13,663 --> 00:15:14,746
Okay.

195
00:15:14,747 --> 00:15:16,582
GUIDE TO WINNING CEO KANG HA-GI
CROSS OUT CHOCOLATE LATTE

196
00:15:18,126 --> 00:15:21,878
I think he spends time on the rooftop
right after eating lunch.

197
00:15:21,879 --> 00:15:24,756
He likes to spend at least 20 minutes
a day in the sun.

198
00:15:24,757 --> 00:15:26,092
GUIDE TO WINNING CEO KANG HA-GI
BE SUNLIGHT BUDDIES

199
00:15:33,766 --> 00:15:37,687
Oh, my.
I didn't know you came here too.

200
00:15:37,812 --> 00:15:39,479
Great view, isn't it?

201
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:40,523
Yes.

202
00:15:41,899 --> 00:15:45,026
I always get my share of sunlight

203
00:15:45,027 --> 00:15:46,945
whenever I'm done with lunch.

204
00:15:46,946 --> 00:15:49,490
People need sunlight to stay healthy.

205
00:15:49,866 --> 00:15:53,535
Mr. Kang, people these days
are often low on vitamin D.

206
00:15:53,536 --> 00:15:55,163
- Ms. Nam.
- Yes?

207
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:03,129
You're very distracting.
And don't stand in my view.

208
00:16:06,174 --> 00:16:07,175
Right.

209
00:16:07,592 --> 00:16:08,759
I'm sorry.

210
00:16:11,137 --> 00:16:12,930
GUIDE TO WINNING CEO KANG HA-GI
CROSS OUT SUNLIGHT BUDDIES

211
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:17,142
Also, when you compliment him
on his style

212
00:16:17,143 --> 00:16:18,602
he gets somewhat pleased.

213
00:16:18,603 --> 00:16:20,104
GUIDE TO WINNING CEO KANG HA-GI
COMPLIMENT HIM

214
00:16:21,230 --> 00:16:23,815
My gosh, Mr. Kang.

215
00:16:23,816 --> 00:16:27,569
You look so cool
in that shirt and tie.

216
00:16:27,570 --> 00:16:29,070
You could be a runway model.

217
00:16:29,071 --> 00:16:31,073
I pulled an all-nighter,
so it's the same as yesterday.

218
00:16:35,870 --> 00:16:37,121
Goodbye.

219
00:16:40,416 --> 00:16:41,833
GUIDE TO WINNING CEO KANG HA-GI
CROSS OUT COMPLIMENTS

220
00:16:41,834 --> 00:16:44,045
How come nothing is working?

221
00:16:53,763 --> 00:16:57,058
You look so cool
in that shirt and tie.

222
00:16:57,475 --> 00:16:58,893
You could be a runway model.

223
00:17:06,359 --> 00:17:07,443
My gosh.

224
00:17:13,824 --> 00:17:15,992
I looked into Ms. Nam

225
00:17:15,993 --> 00:17:17,744
and she recently quit...

226
00:17:17,745 --> 00:17:19,997
Just speak normally.
It's just the two of us here.

227
00:17:20,456 --> 00:17:21,540
Yes, sir.

228
00:17:21,541 --> 00:17:24,961
Ms. Nam recently resigned
from her job at SE Corporation.

229
00:17:26,754 --> 00:17:30,258
I feel like she has a hidden agenda.

230
00:17:30,550 --> 00:17:32,717
Maybe she's a honey trap

231
00:17:32,718 --> 00:17:33,761
sent by Director Kim.

232
00:17:35,763 --> 00:17:36,806
Honey trap?

233
00:17:37,682 --> 00:17:38,765
I don't think so.

234
00:17:38,766 --> 00:17:40,309
Exactly. It's nonsense.

235
00:17:41,477 --> 00:17:44,021
How about a cuteness ploy?
Someone who traps you with cuteness.

236
00:17:47,650 --> 00:17:48,859
That also doesn't make sense.

237
00:17:49,235 --> 00:17:50,653
Is she here just to wreak havoc?

238
00:18:01,163 --> 00:18:04,166
How do I get on Mr. Kang's good side?

239
00:18:04,750 --> 00:18:06,460
- What's up?
- I mean

240
00:18:06,961 --> 00:18:10,547
whenever I say something,
all he says is, "No, thanks."

241
00:18:10,548 --> 00:18:13,466
There's no way to get through to him.

242
00:18:13,467 --> 00:18:15,302
It's not like I'm into him.

243
00:18:15,303 --> 00:18:16,886
I'm trying to be
the outstanding employee.

244
00:18:16,887 --> 00:18:19,264
Maybe he thinks
you're hitting on him.

245
00:18:19,265 --> 00:18:22,142
He just doesn't let anyone
get close to him.

246
00:18:22,143 --> 00:18:23,894
Is that why he shuts you off?

247
00:18:24,437 --> 00:18:26,605
No, he's like that
to everyone else too.

248
00:18:26,606 --> 00:18:28,356
That's why the employees

249
00:18:28,357 --> 00:18:30,692
nicknamed him Icy Kang.

250
00:18:30,693 --> 00:18:32,068
He's that cold.

251
00:18:32,069 --> 00:18:34,696
Hey, look at this.

252
00:18:34,697 --> 00:18:37,407
Exclusive! Former K-pop idol
and top actor A is allegedly gay.

253
00:18:37,408 --> 00:18:39,492
The boyfriend, B, is the current CEO
of his fashion platform.

254
00:18:39,493 --> 00:18:41,578
Rumors say he hired him
to keep their relationship secret.

255
00:18:41,579 --> 00:18:43,204
No way. That's obviously Appello.

256
00:18:43,205 --> 00:18:44,289
Totes. It's Appello.

257
00:18:44,290 --> 00:18:46,166
Wow, Lee Chan is gay?

258
00:18:46,167 --> 00:18:48,419
- He's gay?
- He's gay?

259
00:18:49,170 --> 00:18:52,923
Hey, are A and B here referring

260
00:18:53,215 --> 00:18:54,884
- to Chan and your CEO?
- What?

261
00:18:55,468 --> 00:18:56,469
What?

262
00:18:56,844 --> 00:18:57,845
Are they dating?

263
00:18:58,471 --> 00:18:59,972
What are you talking about?

264
00:19:00,514 --> 00:19:01,599
Chan is...

265
00:19:03,392 --> 00:19:04,726
a heterosexual.

266
00:19:04,727 --> 00:19:07,312
He once said in an interview
that an older girl at his high school

267
00:19:07,313 --> 00:19:08,606
was his first love.

268
00:19:09,148 --> 00:19:10,231
Then what is this?

269
00:19:10,232 --> 00:19:12,860
What do you think? A blind item
circulating in the financial world.

270
00:19:13,653 --> 00:19:16,113
Our company CEO and Chan?

271
00:19:16,614 --> 00:19:17,865
No way.

272
00:19:23,454 --> 00:19:24,789
No, impossible.

273
00:20:08,249 --> 00:20:09,792
Oh, come on.

274
00:20:18,134 --> 00:20:19,760
Hey, get up and eat.

275
00:20:34,191 --> 00:20:35,901
Yes, this is what I'm talking about.

276
00:20:36,444 --> 00:20:38,028
Wait, aren't you eating?

277
00:20:38,696 --> 00:20:40,072
This is how I eat breakfast.

278
00:20:41,449 --> 00:20:44,702
Hey, grabbing a drink was an excuse.
You came to eat that, right?

279
00:20:45,703 --> 00:20:46,704
Bingo.

280
00:20:51,083 --> 00:20:53,877
Gosh, yes. That hits the spot.

281
00:20:53,878 --> 00:20:55,880
It tastes just like your mother's...

282
00:21:06,849 --> 00:21:09,310
Gosh, it's so filling
to finally eat a home-cooked meal.

283
00:21:10,060 --> 00:21:11,519
Can I stay at your place for a while?

284
00:21:11,520 --> 00:21:14,481
No, I had to sleep on the couch,
and my back is killing me.

285
00:21:14,482 --> 00:21:15,608
We could've shared the bed.

286
00:21:17,401 --> 00:21:18,402
Are you insane?

287
00:21:19,403 --> 00:21:20,737
I'm running late.

288
00:21:20,738 --> 00:21:21,989
Eat, clean up, and go.

289
00:21:23,073 --> 00:21:24,074
Hey.

290
00:21:24,950 --> 00:21:26,994
Take this. You haven't even eaten.

291
00:21:27,578 --> 00:21:29,955
- What's this?
- I got it from someone I work with.

292
00:21:30,539 --> 00:21:31,999
It should be good.
If anything, they know good food.

293
00:21:32,750 --> 00:21:33,793
Take it.

294
00:21:36,295 --> 00:21:37,796
- Bye.
- Bye.

295
00:21:37,797 --> 00:21:38,881
Clean up before you go!

296
00:21:42,885 --> 00:21:44,220
CEO KANG HA-GI

297
00:22:50,494 --> 00:22:51,495
Come in.

298
00:22:51,912 --> 00:22:54,539
Mr. Kang, the weekly meeting
for the marketing team is ready.

299
00:22:54,540 --> 00:22:56,333
- Okay. I'll be there.
- Yes, sir.

300
00:23:16,186 --> 00:23:17,438
Jeez.

301
00:23:22,401 --> 00:23:25,069
Hey, come and take these now.

302
00:23:25,070 --> 00:23:27,697
Yes, for this lookbook shooting

303
00:23:27,698 --> 00:23:30,617
we want to focus on gorpcore

304
00:23:30,618 --> 00:23:33,621
as that is the trending aesthetic
at the moment.

305
00:23:40,628 --> 00:23:42,921
Hobbies that are on the rise

306
00:23:42,922 --> 00:23:46,383
include hiking, tennis, and running.

307
00:23:46,759 --> 00:23:50,428
But the outfits
for these hobbies look too sporty.

308
00:23:50,429 --> 00:23:51,430
So?

309
00:23:51,931 --> 00:23:52,932
What's your point?

310
00:23:54,642 --> 00:23:56,143
- Sorry?
- The key point.

311
00:23:57,186 --> 00:23:58,187
The key point...

312
00:24:04,151 --> 00:24:07,071
The visual concept
for the next season

313
00:24:07,821 --> 00:24:09,073
is camping.

314
00:24:10,866 --> 00:24:11,992
Okay, camping.

315
00:24:12,785 --> 00:24:14,035
Sounds great.

316
00:24:14,036 --> 00:24:15,162
From now on

317
00:24:16,038 --> 00:24:18,666
please do not spend
over a minute on your presentation.

318
00:24:19,124 --> 00:24:21,000
I'm not looking for

319
00:24:21,001 --> 00:24:24,171
an elaborate speech,
but the actual result of your work.

320
00:24:26,090 --> 00:24:27,257
Yes, sir.

321
00:24:27,716 --> 00:24:28,968
Are we done here?

322
00:24:29,468 --> 00:24:31,512
- Yes.
- This week

323
00:24:31,929 --> 00:24:33,889
I expect everyone to go all-in
on the Appello fashion show.

324
00:24:34,390 --> 00:24:36,099
It would be nice to film
what the venue is like

325
00:24:36,100 --> 00:24:38,017
and upload it to our official
social media accounts.

326
00:24:38,018 --> 00:24:39,019
Any volunteers?

327
00:24:43,774 --> 00:24:47,527
Lastly, Mr. Kang likes
those who take the initiative.

328
00:24:47,528 --> 00:24:49,738
Someone who steps up
and tries to make things happen.

329
00:24:50,197 --> 00:24:51,281
I will

330
00:24:51,782 --> 00:24:52,783
do it.

331
00:24:55,035 --> 00:24:57,912
Other people have a lot of work to do

332
00:24:57,913 --> 00:24:59,331
so I'll do it.

333
00:24:59,832 --> 00:25:01,582
Yes, she has been assisting

334
00:25:01,583 --> 00:25:03,918
with the management
of our social media account

335
00:25:03,919 --> 00:25:05,129
so it'll help.

336
00:25:09,675 --> 00:25:10,676
All right, then.

337
00:25:12,928 --> 00:25:14,346
We'll go and see the rehearsal today

338
00:25:14,805 --> 00:25:16,848
so be at my office by two o'clock.

339
00:25:16,849 --> 00:25:17,850
Yes, sir.

340
00:25:18,726 --> 00:25:20,310
Hey, Da-reum.

341
00:25:20,728 --> 00:25:23,605
It's your first time on site.
Are you sure you'll be fine?

342
00:25:25,315 --> 00:25:26,525
Mr. Kang.

343
00:25:27,860 --> 00:25:30,194
I think I should probably go.

344
00:25:30,195 --> 00:25:31,405
Let's give the volunteer a try.

345
00:25:34,283 --> 00:25:35,366
That's all, then.

346
00:25:35,367 --> 00:25:36,452
- Yes.
- Yes.

347
00:25:38,954 --> 00:25:39,955
Good luck.

348
00:26:05,230 --> 00:26:06,273
Mr. Kang...

349
00:26:23,665 --> 00:26:25,125
Everything is so neatly organized

350
00:26:26,085 --> 00:26:27,795
as expected from the office's owner.

351
00:26:29,922 --> 00:26:31,757
I can't believe I spent a night here.

352
00:26:43,727 --> 00:26:46,355
I want to be an outstanding employee
to join this trip.

353
00:26:54,488 --> 00:26:56,115
Wait, what?

354
00:26:57,407 --> 00:26:59,326
Why is he

355
00:26:59,952 --> 00:27:01,286
looking at him like that?

356
00:27:24,476 --> 00:27:25,727
What can I do

357
00:27:26,228 --> 00:27:28,313
to show you how I feel?

358
00:27:29,148 --> 00:27:31,233
I love you, Chan.

359
00:27:31,567 --> 00:27:34,862
- I love you, Chan.
- "I love you, Chan"?

360
00:27:59,011 --> 00:28:00,262
What can I do

361
00:28:01,180 --> 00:28:03,140
to show you how I feel?

362
00:28:05,267 --> 00:28:06,268
I love you...

363
00:28:08,562 --> 00:28:09,730
Chan.

364
00:28:17,779 --> 00:28:19,156
That blind item

365
00:28:20,449 --> 00:28:21,742
must be true.

366
00:28:24,411 --> 00:28:26,163
What do I do? What now?

367
00:28:38,217 --> 00:28:39,551
NO IMPORTANT DOCUMENT ON THE DESK

368
00:28:39,885 --> 00:28:41,678
- Did you wait long?
- Sorry?

369
00:28:42,346 --> 00:28:43,596
No, I just got here.

370
00:28:43,597 --> 00:28:47,684
I left the weekly meeting report
on your desk, sir.

371
00:28:59,529 --> 00:29:00,697
NO LEAKAGE OF CONFIDENTIAL INFO

372
00:29:07,120 --> 00:29:08,371
- Let's go.
- Sorry?

373
00:29:08,372 --> 00:29:10,290
Right. Yes.

374
00:29:10,874 --> 00:29:11,875
Let's go.

375
00:29:26,431 --> 00:29:27,432
- These days,
- Yes?

376
00:29:30,644 --> 00:29:32,354
is the job market tough?

377
00:29:34,731 --> 00:29:38,026
Yes, that's the case.

378
00:29:39,278 --> 00:29:42,113
Someone with your credentials
could've gone to major corporations.

379
00:29:42,114 --> 00:29:43,115
Gosh, hardly.

380
00:29:44,074 --> 00:29:45,158
By any chance

381
00:29:46,243 --> 00:29:48,328
any special reason
why you came to Appello?

382
00:29:51,748 --> 00:29:54,960
Actually, I wanted
to learn more about myself.

383
00:29:55,419 --> 00:29:57,086
Instead of just getting
more qualifications

384
00:29:57,087 --> 00:30:00,007
I wanted to find out
what I truly love.

385
00:30:00,257 --> 00:30:03,468
That was why I chose
to come to a place I was drawn to.

386
00:30:04,803 --> 00:30:05,846
Also

387
00:30:06,805 --> 00:30:10,142
there was someone
I really wanted to meet.

388
00:30:12,602 --> 00:30:13,770
Who is it?

389
00:30:15,439 --> 00:30:16,440
What?

390
00:30:18,567 --> 00:30:19,859
Did I just say it out loud?

391
00:30:19,860 --> 00:30:21,278
That was why I heard it.

392
00:30:26,450 --> 00:30:28,118
Well, what I meant

393
00:30:28,994 --> 00:30:32,455
was that I wanted to meet many people
in different industries on the job.

394
00:30:32,456 --> 00:30:33,832
Something like that.

395
00:30:38,086 --> 00:30:41,298
Mr. Kang, may I ask something too?

396
00:30:42,632 --> 00:30:43,633
Sure.

397
00:30:43,967 --> 00:30:46,803
Why did you come to Appello?

398
00:30:51,433 --> 00:30:54,269
At first,
it was because of one person.

399
00:30:55,020 --> 00:30:58,022
Could that be Chan?

400
00:30:58,023 --> 00:31:00,901
But now, Appello is my everything.

401
00:31:33,850 --> 00:31:35,768
- What's this? A prize draw?
- It's a prize draw.

402
00:31:35,769 --> 00:31:36,770
Thank you.

403
00:31:41,400 --> 00:31:42,526
My gosh. So that's how it looks.

404
00:31:44,319 --> 00:31:45,404
That's cool.

405
00:31:54,371 --> 00:31:55,872
That is so awesome.

406
00:31:57,416 --> 00:31:59,292
Is she putting on a show,
trying to look innocent?

407
00:32:00,836 --> 00:32:02,587
Goodness, Mr. Kang!

408
00:32:03,296 --> 00:32:06,341
I can't believe
you came all the way here yourself.

409
00:32:07,008 --> 00:32:08,802
- Hello.
- Of course, I should come.

410
00:32:09,052 --> 00:32:10,261
How's it coming along?

411
00:32:10,262 --> 00:32:11,430
Yes, of course.

412
00:32:12,013 --> 00:32:14,306
A new brand like ours
could never even dream

413
00:32:14,307 --> 00:32:15,516
of having a fashion show.

414
00:32:15,517 --> 00:32:17,978
Thank you very much
for giving us this great opportunity.

415
00:32:18,186 --> 00:32:20,896
Don't mention it.
Your brand already had the appeal.

416
00:32:20,897 --> 00:32:21,940
The opportunity simply found you.

417
00:32:23,442 --> 00:32:25,694
Anyway, I've never seen those before.

418
00:32:27,070 --> 00:32:30,031
This kind of event is a rare chance.

419
00:32:31,283 --> 00:32:34,953
So we even took out a loan
to make lots of new products.

420
00:32:35,871 --> 00:32:37,621
Although we wouldn't survive

421
00:32:37,622 --> 00:32:39,708
until the next season
if they end up as inventory.

422
00:32:40,292 --> 00:32:42,334
Oh, I almost jinxed it. Never mind.

423
00:32:42,335 --> 00:32:43,711
I won't let that happen.

424
00:32:43,712 --> 00:32:46,046
I'll make sure

425
00:32:46,047 --> 00:32:49,675
people see our products
- and immediately go, "It's Go.
- Co."

426
00:32:49,676 --> 00:32:51,302
I will make it happen.

427
00:32:51,303 --> 00:32:52,512
I can do it!

428
00:32:53,054 --> 00:32:54,972
- Yes, please keep up the good work.
- Thanks.

429
00:32:54,973 --> 00:32:56,056
See you at the show.

430
00:32:56,057 --> 00:32:58,268
All right. Keep it up, Mr. Kang!

431
00:32:58,602 --> 00:32:59,811
- Let's go!
- Go for it!

432
00:33:06,276 --> 00:33:07,277
What are you smiling about?

433
00:33:09,946 --> 00:33:12,573
I had a thought that fashion brands

434
00:33:12,574 --> 00:33:15,076
and K-pop idol groups are similar.

435
00:33:15,994 --> 00:33:17,537
- K-pop idol?
- Yes.

436
00:33:18,538 --> 00:33:20,706
They show their presence on the stage

437
00:33:20,707 --> 00:33:23,417
bring thrills to people
with their visuals

438
00:33:23,418 --> 00:33:26,087
and above all, they're loved
by their fans for a very long time.

439
00:33:30,759 --> 00:33:33,302
Everyone must've put in
so much hard work

440
00:33:33,303 --> 00:33:35,514
just to get their chance
on that stage.

441
00:33:37,724 --> 00:33:39,893
I really hope this fashion show

442
00:33:40,393 --> 00:33:41,811
becomes a huge hit.

443
00:33:42,938 --> 00:33:45,190
I'll put in everything I have too.

444
00:34:02,415 --> 00:34:04,709
Now, let us begin!

445
00:34:05,168 --> 00:34:07,419
The first model, walk up to the spot.

446
00:34:07,420 --> 00:34:09,756
Maintain a three-second interval.
Now, go!

447
00:34:27,107 --> 00:34:28,650
Cool.

448
00:34:39,244 --> 00:34:40,578
- What happened?
- Cut.

449
00:34:40,579 --> 00:34:41,787
Are you okay?

450
00:34:41,788 --> 00:34:44,708
- Hey, go check on the model.
- Yes, sir.

451
00:34:45,500 --> 00:34:47,586
Reduce the amount of dry ice.

452
00:34:48,628 --> 00:34:51,922
- Was it because of dry ice?
- Yes, it looks like it.

453
00:34:51,923 --> 00:34:54,050
If too much dry ice is used,
it creates vapors.

454
00:34:58,471 --> 00:35:02,016
That's why he almost fell
on stage before.

455
00:35:02,017 --> 00:35:03,642
Let's wipe the stage.

456
00:35:03,643 --> 00:35:05,352
Can I have someone test the stage
before we begin?

457
00:35:05,353 --> 00:35:07,105
Anyone wearing dress shoes
among the staff?

458
00:35:13,737 --> 00:35:14,820
Can I do it?

459
00:35:14,821 --> 00:35:17,240
These heels are pretty low.
I think these will be okay.

460
00:35:17,866 --> 00:35:21,035
- Can I ask you to do it then?
- Of course.

461
00:35:21,036 --> 00:35:22,786
Why would you?

462
00:35:22,787 --> 00:35:24,622
If models get hurt, that will cause
problems for the show.

463
00:35:24,623 --> 00:35:26,498
I'll go walk slowly.

464
00:35:26,499 --> 00:35:29,377
- Do I start behind the stage?
- Yes. Thank you.

465
00:35:48,355 --> 00:35:49,564
Oh, no.

466
00:35:56,821 --> 00:35:57,822
Ms. Nam!

467
00:36:23,890 --> 00:36:25,475
- Are you okay?
- Yes.

468
00:36:26,184 --> 00:36:27,894
Oh, yes. I'm okay.

469
00:36:28,728 --> 00:36:31,730
You should've just walked.
Why did you make a turn?

470
00:36:31,731 --> 00:36:33,692
You almost hurt your head
from your carelessness.

471
00:36:35,902 --> 00:36:37,821
I know. Why did I do that?

472
00:36:40,573 --> 00:36:42,783
It's a bit watery over here.

473
00:36:42,784 --> 00:36:45,452
Someone should wipe over here.

474
00:36:45,453 --> 00:36:47,872
- Okay. Hey, go wipe it.
- Yes.

475
00:36:55,380 --> 00:36:58,257
We have Lee Chan playing the role

476
00:36:58,258 --> 00:37:00,843
of Seong-jun who appears
to be perfect in every way

477
00:37:00,844 --> 00:37:02,803
but actually clumsy and vulnerable
when it comes to love

478
00:37:02,804 --> 00:37:07,474
and Yoon Cho-yi who plays the role
of Yi-seo who matures by experiencing

479
00:37:07,475 --> 00:37:09,393
the sweetest moment
as well as the most bitter breakup.

480
00:37:09,394 --> 00:37:12,105
The two lead roles of Bitter Sweet.
Can you please make a heart?

481
00:37:14,524 --> 00:37:15,942
Can you look to the left?

482
00:37:16,484 --> 00:37:17,527
Now, to the center.

483
00:37:17,986 --> 00:37:19,070
To the right, please.

484
00:37:19,821 --> 00:37:21,281
Very nice.

485
00:37:22,574 --> 00:37:24,324
It's time for questions.

486
00:37:24,325 --> 00:37:26,785
If you have any questions,
please raise your hands

487
00:37:26,786 --> 00:37:28,079
and we'll pass you the mic.

488
00:37:28,705 --> 00:37:30,456
- Yes?
- Your unique chemistry was

489
00:37:30,457 --> 00:37:32,750
already evident in the preview.

490
00:37:32,751 --> 00:37:34,501
I wonder if you grew any feelings
for each other

491
00:37:34,502 --> 00:37:37,130
while working on this film.

492
00:37:37,422 --> 00:37:41,593
Well, to be honest, who wouldn't be
fluttered to see Lee Chan?

493
00:37:42,218 --> 00:37:45,095
I've been a fan of his
for a long time

494
00:37:45,096 --> 00:37:47,891
so that helped me focus
on portraying my emotions.

495
00:37:50,477 --> 00:37:52,103
Well, Ms. Cho-yi is very lovely.

496
00:37:52,562 --> 00:37:54,772
I think this drama did a good job

497
00:37:54,773 --> 00:37:56,815
of showcasing her charms.

498
00:37:56,816 --> 00:38:00,069
If I meet someone like her
in real life

499
00:38:01,905 --> 00:38:03,740
I can't help but fall in love.

500
00:38:07,827 --> 00:38:10,580
LEE CHAN AND YOON CHO-YI
GETTING FLUTTERED WHILE FILMING?

501
00:38:12,165 --> 00:38:14,041
Good job today.

502
00:38:14,042 --> 00:38:15,542
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

503
00:38:15,543 --> 00:38:16,668
See you later.

504
00:38:16,669 --> 00:38:18,087
- Bye.
- Bye.

505
00:38:21,800 --> 00:38:23,510
Good work, Mr. Lee.

506
00:38:24,093 --> 00:38:25,345
Yes, good work.

507
00:38:31,684 --> 00:38:32,936
Give me a second.

508
00:38:39,901 --> 00:38:42,529
Did you receive the gift I sent you?

509
00:38:43,154 --> 00:38:44,614
I gave it to my friend.

510
00:38:45,031 --> 00:38:46,032
What?

511
00:38:48,117 --> 00:38:50,578
You've been ignoring my calls.
How long will you keep doing this?

512
00:38:50,995 --> 00:38:52,038
Cho-yi.

513
00:38:53,790 --> 00:38:54,833
We broke up.

514
00:38:55,667 --> 00:38:57,544
- It's time for you to accept it.
- No.

515
00:38:58,628 --> 00:39:02,048
I can't break up with you.
No, I'm not breaking up with you.

516
00:39:02,924 --> 00:39:04,800
I really loved you.

517
00:39:04,801 --> 00:39:06,302
Are you saying you didn't love me?

518
00:39:07,220 --> 00:39:08,346
Not even for a moment?

519
00:39:08,680 --> 00:39:10,181
I did have feelings for you.

520
00:39:10,765 --> 00:39:13,517
But it wasn't love.

521
00:39:13,518 --> 00:39:14,686
But why?

522
00:39:15,603 --> 00:39:17,230
What do I lack?

523
00:39:19,691 --> 00:39:21,526
It's not that you lacked anything.

524
00:39:21,818 --> 00:39:23,361
We just weren't right for each other.

525
00:39:23,862 --> 00:39:24,863
Cho-yi.

526
00:39:26,239 --> 00:39:29,534
You're perfect
just the way you are, okay?

527
00:39:34,372 --> 00:39:37,709
Do you know how much I struggled
and endured to put up with you?

528
00:39:38,459 --> 00:39:39,877
Are you saying
I wasn't right for you?

529
00:39:39,878 --> 00:39:42,422
Do you think all that struggling
and enduring means love?

530
00:39:44,132 --> 00:39:46,551
Someone who lets you be yourself.

531
00:39:47,886 --> 00:39:49,095
Find someone like that.

532
00:39:51,806 --> 00:39:53,265
This is ridiculous.

533
00:39:53,266 --> 00:39:55,602
You pretend to be polite and sweet.

534
00:39:56,436 --> 00:39:58,771
But you're just pretending
to be the better person to leave me.

535
00:40:00,023 --> 00:40:01,024
...I

536
00:40:02,275 --> 00:40:03,735
I won't ever break up with you.

537
00:40:04,986 --> 00:40:06,279
So...

538
00:40:07,655 --> 00:40:08,948
you might as well endure it.

539
00:40:48,237 --> 00:40:51,074
Well, should I play some music?

540
00:40:51,783 --> 00:40:53,117
Oh, yes. I'd love that.

541
00:40:58,164 --> 00:40:59,332
What...

542
00:41:01,334 --> 00:41:03,378
Why is this...

543
00:41:07,840 --> 00:41:08,841
INCOMING CALL
LEE CHAN

544
00:41:12,470 --> 00:41:13,721
ANSWER

545
00:41:14,263 --> 00:41:15,848
- Hello?
- Where are you?

546
00:41:16,724 --> 00:41:18,141
It's really Chan.

547
00:41:18,142 --> 00:41:20,103
I'm almost at work. Where are you?

548
00:41:20,436 --> 00:41:22,522
Me? Not sure.

549
00:41:23,523 --> 00:41:25,984
What? We spent all night together.
But do you miss me already?

550
00:41:26,734 --> 00:41:28,027
"All night"?

551
00:41:32,281 --> 00:41:34,574
Hey, stop joking around, will you?

552
00:41:34,575 --> 00:41:37,745
What? We were good together
until this morning.

553
00:41:38,121 --> 00:41:39,621
Until this morning?

554
00:41:39,622 --> 00:41:41,164
By the way,
what am I supposed to pick up?

555
00:41:41,165 --> 00:41:42,791
Whatever. I'll throw it out.

556
00:41:42,792 --> 00:41:44,002
You're better off without seeing it.

557
00:41:48,464 --> 00:41:52,051
What can I do to show you how I feel?

558
00:41:52,802 --> 00:41:54,762
I love you, Chan.

559
00:42:01,477 --> 00:42:04,814
Is he throwing out that card?

560
00:42:07,650 --> 00:42:09,235
The power is off.

561
00:42:47,398 --> 00:42:48,691
I can't believe

562
00:42:49,734 --> 00:42:51,652
Mr. Kang was in love with Chan.

563
00:42:56,157 --> 00:42:58,659
How did I end up
finding out this secret?

564
00:43:01,954 --> 00:43:02,955
You're still here?

565
00:43:34,070 --> 00:43:35,612
Director Lee.

566
00:43:35,613 --> 00:43:36,697
Have you been well?

567
00:43:39,534 --> 00:43:40,535
Yes.

568
00:43:43,830 --> 00:43:45,123
Oh, hello.

569
00:43:49,836 --> 00:43:52,839
Who was your favorite in D.N.X?

570
00:43:53,131 --> 00:43:54,382
Well...

571
00:43:55,299 --> 00:43:56,300
Pardon?

572
00:43:58,010 --> 00:43:59,427
How did you know that?

573
00:43:59,428 --> 00:44:01,472
You're listening to our song
from ten years ago.

574
00:44:09,147 --> 00:44:10,481
By any chance...

575
00:44:14,026 --> 00:44:15,153
was it me?

576
00:44:25,246 --> 00:44:26,247
Right?

577
00:44:28,749 --> 00:44:29,750
It was.

578
00:44:30,918 --> 00:44:32,210
I'm doomed.

579
00:44:32,211 --> 00:44:33,421
Gosh...

580
00:44:37,258 --> 00:44:40,344
How did you get that right
on your first try?

581
00:44:40,636 --> 00:44:42,930
Just my gut feeling.

582
00:44:46,184 --> 00:44:48,811
Oh, my gosh. That's crazy.

583
00:44:50,897 --> 00:44:53,107
You must've been a fan
since you were a kid.

584
00:44:54,567 --> 00:44:56,443
You can call me Chan
when it's just the two of us.

585
00:44:56,444 --> 00:44:58,154
Oh, no. Still...

586
00:44:58,529 --> 00:44:59,906
I will

587
00:45:01,365 --> 00:45:03,284
call you Da-reum.
Is that okay with you?

588
00:45:07,914 --> 00:45:08,915
Yes.

589
00:45:10,082 --> 00:45:11,250
Chan.

590
00:45:14,962 --> 00:45:18,089
It's been over ten years
since D.N.X disbanded.

591
00:45:18,090 --> 00:45:20,259
I didn't know there was still someone
who listened to our music.

592
00:45:21,010 --> 00:45:22,011
Thank you.

593
00:45:24,138 --> 00:45:27,307
I've listened to it for so long

594
00:45:27,308 --> 00:45:29,101
that it's become part of my routine.

595
00:45:29,477 --> 00:45:31,103
When I'm walking or working

596
00:45:32,438 --> 00:45:34,982
I find myself listening to it
without even realizing it.

597
00:45:36,192 --> 00:45:38,027
NAM DA-REUM

598
00:45:42,823 --> 00:45:44,617
- Give me your phone.
- What?

599
00:45:53,167 --> 00:45:55,127
I left it in the office.

600
00:46:33,749 --> 00:46:34,792
There.

601
00:46:41,841 --> 00:46:42,842
Call me.

602
00:46:46,595 --> 00:46:47,596
I will.

603
00:46:52,768 --> 00:46:53,853
You promise?

604
00:46:58,691 --> 00:47:00,276
No way.

605
00:47:01,068 --> 00:47:02,069
Awesome.

606
00:47:02,820 --> 00:47:05,031
Is this really Chan's number?

607
00:47:06,115 --> 00:47:07,116
Yes.

608
00:47:07,742 --> 00:47:10,244
Hey. Namda.

609
00:47:12,038 --> 00:47:13,414
She's completely out of it.

610
00:47:13,706 --> 00:47:15,249
A celeb giving you his number?

611
00:47:15,458 --> 00:47:16,751
What's that supposed to mean?

612
00:47:17,043 --> 00:47:19,253
He told you to call him.
Call him and find out.

613
00:47:21,088 --> 00:47:24,132
I doubt he really meant it.

614
00:47:24,133 --> 00:47:26,385
It's just that I work for his company

615
00:47:27,011 --> 00:47:28,595
and I'm an old fan, so...

616
00:47:28,596 --> 00:47:29,597
So?

617
00:47:32,099 --> 00:47:33,391
Oh, I don't know.

618
00:47:33,392 --> 00:47:36,728
Maybe he gave it to you
because he had a crush on you.

619
00:47:36,729 --> 00:47:38,522
- What?
- She's right.

620
00:47:38,856 --> 00:47:40,815
He could've saved your number
on his phone.

621
00:47:40,816 --> 00:47:42,609
Why did he have to do that?

622
00:47:42,610 --> 00:47:44,027
Why did he write it on your hand?

623
00:47:44,028 --> 00:47:45,278
He was totally flirting.

624
00:47:45,279 --> 00:47:48,783
Hey. He wasn't.
That's totally not true.

625
00:47:49,200 --> 00:47:50,201
First things first.

626
00:47:51,702 --> 00:47:52,703
Let's save it.

627
00:47:54,538 --> 00:47:55,748
Don't do anything other than saving.

628
00:48:03,839 --> 00:48:06,132
What the? Are you really calling him?

629
00:48:06,133 --> 00:48:07,550
Hey. No. Stop it.

630
00:48:07,551 --> 00:48:10,220
Are you nuts? Get back here.
Give it to me.

631
00:48:10,221 --> 00:48:11,389
Hey.

632
00:48:13,891 --> 00:48:16,352
What do I do? What am I going to say?

633
00:48:20,147 --> 00:48:21,440
Hello?

634
00:48:25,611 --> 00:48:27,320
Chan?

635
00:48:27,321 --> 00:48:30,116
It's me, Da-reum.

636
00:48:32,243 --> 00:48:33,452
Hello?

637
00:48:41,752 --> 00:48:44,130
Isn't this Director Lee's number?

638
00:48:44,547 --> 00:48:45,756
Director Lee?

639
00:48:46,799 --> 00:48:48,509
Yes, this is his number.

640
00:48:52,263 --> 00:48:57,058
I work for Director Lee's company.

641
00:48:57,059 --> 00:48:59,812
Oh, my Chan?

642
00:49:00,396 --> 00:49:01,730
He's in the shower.

643
00:49:07,945 --> 00:49:09,155
Sorry about that.

644
00:49:13,534 --> 00:49:16,245
Saying you work for him
after calling him Chan?

645
00:49:16,996 --> 00:49:18,079
That's beyond ridiculous.

646
00:49:18,080 --> 00:49:19,623
DELETE THIS CONTACT?

647
00:49:24,211 --> 00:49:25,545
BITTER SWEET

648
00:49:25,546 --> 00:49:26,796
What's the next scene?

649
00:49:26,797 --> 00:49:28,632
Prepare it thoroughly...

650
00:49:34,889 --> 00:49:36,473
What are you doing in my green room?

651
00:49:36,474 --> 00:49:37,600
The next scene.

652
00:49:38,267 --> 00:49:39,602
Will you help me rehearse?

653
00:49:41,562 --> 00:49:42,854
We still need to do our job.

654
00:49:42,855 --> 00:49:44,190
- Do you want to grab coffee?
- Let's get coffee.

655
00:49:52,781 --> 00:49:53,782
Namda.

656
00:49:57,036 --> 00:49:59,621
I told you not to call him. See?

657
00:49:59,622 --> 00:50:02,957
Why did he lead you on
when he has a girlfriend?

658
00:50:02,958 --> 00:50:04,460
I told you it wasn't like that.

659
00:50:04,752 --> 00:50:06,795
You're the same.

660
00:50:08,214 --> 00:50:10,466
Look what you've done.

661
00:50:10,966 --> 00:50:12,510
I'm doomed.

662
00:50:13,052 --> 00:50:15,221
Oh, I'm doomed.

663
00:50:15,513 --> 00:50:18,389
- It's your fault.
- Why did you do that?

664
00:50:18,390 --> 00:50:21,936
- You called him.
- Because you told me to.

665
00:50:23,312 --> 00:50:24,396
But you know what

666
00:50:25,856 --> 00:50:26,899
this is for the better.

667
00:50:27,608 --> 00:50:30,778
If Chan answered,
it would've been really awkward.

668
00:50:31,153 --> 00:50:32,238
Namda.

669
00:50:33,697 --> 00:50:34,698
You're not disappointed?

670
00:50:36,242 --> 00:50:39,203
Chan is human after all.
Of course, he can have a girlfriend.

671
00:50:39,453 --> 00:50:42,540
I actually want him to meet someone

672
00:50:43,123 --> 00:50:44,291
and be happy.

673
00:50:49,129 --> 00:50:52,591
Hey. A true fan is different.

674
00:50:52,967 --> 00:50:54,677
I approve.

675
00:50:57,012 --> 00:50:58,013
What time is it?

676
00:50:59,014 --> 00:51:00,348
Hey. It's time for Chan's drama.

677
00:51:00,349 --> 00:51:01,809
It's the first episode.
Make sure you stay for it.

678
00:51:20,369 --> 00:51:21,412
Hey.

679
00:51:23,497 --> 00:51:25,207
What's that look on your face?

680
00:51:25,916 --> 00:51:28,085
Are you out of your mind? Hey.

681
00:51:28,460 --> 00:51:30,670
Who are you to be disappointed?

682
00:51:30,671 --> 00:51:32,922
You've been a fan for 12 years.

683
00:51:32,923 --> 00:51:34,258
Get a grip.

684
00:51:44,893 --> 00:51:47,438
What if my call interrupted him?

685
00:51:48,355 --> 00:51:50,524
I hope
he doesn't think I'm a crazy fan.

686
00:51:52,526 --> 00:51:54,486
Oh, forget it.
I don't want to think about it.

687
00:52:09,335 --> 00:52:10,336
Hold on.

688
00:52:10,753 --> 00:52:12,880
I love you, Chan.

689
00:52:15,633 --> 00:52:17,384
If Chan has a girlfriend...

690
00:52:19,762 --> 00:52:21,013
what about Mr. Kang?

691
00:52:24,350 --> 00:52:26,518
Is it one-sided?

692
00:52:30,522 --> 00:52:32,941
That's pitiful.

693
00:52:35,402 --> 00:52:36,528
Oh, gosh.

694
00:52:52,795 --> 00:52:54,838
SUNGJU

695
00:53:14,483 --> 00:53:16,026
Here's your Americano.

696
00:53:18,028 --> 00:53:19,238
Thank you.

697
00:53:41,468 --> 00:53:44,138
How long has he been bottling
his feelings alone?

698
00:53:44,930 --> 00:53:46,098
Did he want to stay by his side

699
00:53:46,598 --> 00:53:48,225
even as a friend?

700
00:54:08,203 --> 00:54:10,581
Mr. Kang, have this

701
00:54:11,248 --> 00:54:12,416
and cheer up.

702
00:54:13,000 --> 00:54:14,001
Good luck.

703
00:54:27,181 --> 00:54:28,265
Mr. Kang.

704
00:54:29,516 --> 00:54:31,852
Mr. Kang. Were you looking for me?

705
00:54:33,395 --> 00:54:34,605
It's been up there for too long.

706
00:54:34,938 --> 00:54:36,398
I've seen it for too long,
it's not so impressive anymore.

707
00:54:37,816 --> 00:54:40,235
Okay, I'll replace it
as soon as possible.

708
00:54:43,781 --> 00:54:46,533
I thought you didn't drink coffee.
What's gotten into you?

709
00:54:47,868 --> 00:54:50,162
Well, it's not so bad.

710
00:54:53,832 --> 00:54:55,167
Good. One, two.

711
00:54:55,584 --> 00:54:58,085
Good. Look at the window. One, two.

712
00:54:58,086 --> 00:54:59,212
Nice.

713
00:54:59,213 --> 00:55:00,339
Fix his hair, please.

714
00:55:01,465 --> 00:55:03,841
Nice. One, two. Smile a bit.

715
00:55:03,842 --> 00:55:05,635
One, two. Excellent.

716
00:55:05,636 --> 00:55:07,095
One more. One, two.

717
00:55:07,471 --> 00:55:08,514
Good job.

718
00:55:09,973 --> 00:55:13,227
- I just love the photos today.
- The colors looked perfect.

719
00:55:14,561 --> 00:55:16,438
- Let me get ready for the next set.
- Okay.

720
00:55:17,481 --> 00:55:19,525
- Hey. Can I have my phone?
- Yes.

721
00:55:21,068 --> 00:55:22,736
- Did I get any calls?
- No.

722
00:55:23,654 --> 00:55:25,030
Are you expecting one?

723
00:55:26,240 --> 00:55:27,406
No.

724
00:55:27,407 --> 00:55:28,991
UNREAD

725
00:55:28,992 --> 00:55:30,577
I just wanted to treat her to a meal.

726
00:55:32,996 --> 00:55:34,998
- Who?
- Just...

727
00:55:36,667 --> 00:55:39,044
Someone I'm grateful to.

728
00:55:41,338 --> 00:55:45,508
Mr. Kang, please confirm the location
for the fashion show.

729
00:55:45,509 --> 00:55:46,510
Sure.

730
00:55:52,349 --> 00:55:54,184
Mr. Kang, do you drink coffee now?

731
00:55:56,979 --> 00:55:59,022
Yes, it happened somehow.

732
00:55:59,857 --> 00:56:01,775
- You may proceed.
- Thank you.

733
00:56:03,068 --> 00:56:04,152
Wait...

734
00:56:04,945 --> 00:56:05,988
Yes, sir.

735
00:56:06,989 --> 00:56:09,116
How is Nam Da-reum doing?

736
00:56:10,200 --> 00:56:11,702
In terms of work and all.

737
00:56:14,037 --> 00:56:15,247
I think

738
00:56:15,664 --> 00:56:17,248
she's very diligent.

739
00:56:17,249 --> 00:56:19,626
She always takes initiative
and does her best in everything.

740
00:56:20,377 --> 00:56:21,920
She's very cheerful.

741
00:56:25,048 --> 00:56:26,299
She actually asked me

742
00:56:26,300 --> 00:56:28,719
about how to become
the outstanding employee.

743
00:56:29,261 --> 00:56:30,429
The outstanding employee?

744
00:56:31,013 --> 00:56:32,014
Yes.

745
00:56:43,567 --> 00:56:45,527
- Are the materials ready?
- Yes.

746
00:56:45,861 --> 00:56:47,821
- Won-tae, let's go.
- Okay.

747
00:56:53,076 --> 00:56:55,870
Da-reum, have you sorted out
the messenger promotion message

748
00:56:55,871 --> 00:56:59,415
- on the Appello fashion show?
- Oh, yes.

749
00:56:59,416 --> 00:57:02,460
I prepared two reminder versions
for the day of the show.

750
00:57:02,461 --> 00:57:03,545
Give me one second.

751
00:57:14,723 --> 00:57:15,933
MESSENGER

752
00:57:17,184 --> 00:57:18,226
NO RESULTS FOUND

753
00:57:20,812 --> 00:57:22,648
- What's taking so long?
- I...

754
00:57:25,067 --> 00:57:26,526
The files are gone.

755
00:57:28,862 --> 00:57:29,988
Gone?

756
00:57:30,322 --> 00:57:31,406
Yes.

757
00:57:34,242 --> 00:57:35,409
I'll make them quickly.

758
00:57:35,410 --> 00:57:37,037
I've already done it once.
It won't take long.

759
00:57:37,412 --> 00:57:40,123
Did you actually do it?

760
00:57:47,089 --> 00:57:50,175
We're updating it tomorrow.
Make sure to send it to me by today.

761
00:57:52,177 --> 00:57:53,428
I'm sorry.

762
00:57:57,975 --> 00:58:01,228
Did someone touch my computer?

763
00:58:01,979 --> 00:58:04,189
No, I doubt it.

764
00:58:05,607 --> 00:58:06,984
I probably lost it.

765
00:58:19,788 --> 00:58:21,206
APPELLO FASHION SHOW
MESSENGER MESSAGE PROPOSAL

766
00:58:25,168 --> 00:58:27,129
I won't have a chance
of becoming an outstanding employee

767
00:58:27,921 --> 00:58:29,673
let alone an ordinary employee.

768
00:58:38,682 --> 00:58:41,059
How can he work overtime every day?

769
00:58:43,562 --> 00:58:45,564
Seriously, that's amazing.

770
00:58:58,577 --> 00:58:59,703
That's strange.

771
00:59:00,287 --> 00:59:03,498
I swear it was on the wallpaper.

772
00:59:08,962 --> 00:59:10,964
What? I'm just borrowing this.

773
00:59:11,923 --> 00:59:12,966
Okay.

774
00:59:26,354 --> 00:59:27,355
No.

775
00:59:27,898 --> 00:59:28,982
Oh, no.

776
00:59:30,901 --> 00:59:32,194
Don't overthink it.

777
00:59:39,493 --> 00:59:41,119
JANGSHINCHEON, GUDORIM

778
01:00:34,422 --> 01:00:37,259
INGUK STATION

779
01:00:38,969 --> 01:00:40,011
Mr. Kang.

780
01:00:40,720 --> 01:00:41,721
Don't you have an umbrella?

781
01:00:42,305 --> 01:00:44,223
What brings you here

782
01:00:44,224 --> 01:00:46,560
- I live around here.
- Really? Me too.

783
01:00:47,060 --> 01:00:48,727
Let's go. I'll walk you home.

784
01:00:48,728 --> 01:00:49,938
Oh, no. It's okay.

785
01:00:50,397 --> 01:00:52,274
- Then will you go on your own?
- What?

786
01:00:53,191 --> 01:00:54,192
No.

787
01:01:04,369 --> 01:01:06,580
What happened to your car?
Why did you take the subway?

788
01:01:07,205 --> 01:01:08,373
It's in the body shop.

789
01:01:10,458 --> 01:01:11,877
Did you work overtime today?

790
01:01:12,878 --> 01:01:14,045
Yes, a little.

791
01:01:15,922 --> 01:01:18,383
If you're getting home now,
it wasn't just a little overtime.

792
01:01:20,177 --> 01:01:21,802
Is there too much work to do?

793
01:01:21,803 --> 01:01:23,221
Oh, no.

794
01:01:23,972 --> 01:01:26,057
It's just that I made a mistake.

795
01:01:28,602 --> 01:01:32,981
I bet you never make any mistakes
because you're thorough.

796
01:01:33,273 --> 01:01:34,649
You're right. I don't.

797
01:01:37,611 --> 01:01:40,322
But I used to make a lot of mistakes
when I was a newbie.

798
01:01:41,823 --> 01:01:44,075
You make mistakes
because you're doing the job.

799
01:01:45,577 --> 01:01:46,912
If you don't do anything

800
01:01:47,537 --> 01:01:48,955
you won't make any mistakes.

801
01:01:50,207 --> 01:01:51,750
Don't be afraid and keep trying

802
01:01:52,751 --> 01:01:53,793
whether it's work

803
01:01:54,419 --> 01:01:55,420
or making mistakes.

804
01:01:59,132 --> 01:02:01,259
Thank you for saying that.

805
01:02:01,885 --> 01:02:03,303
I was actually discouraged until now.

806
01:02:05,305 --> 01:02:08,266
You're more caring than I thought.

807
01:02:09,517 --> 01:02:10,602
Than you thought?

808
01:02:11,269 --> 01:02:15,148
Yes, everyone is afraid of your glare
so they avoid talking to you.

809
01:02:15,523 --> 01:02:16,524
Didn't you know?

810
01:02:24,449 --> 01:02:25,700
What? Wait.

811
01:02:28,328 --> 01:02:29,871
Anyway, this is pretty cool.

812
01:02:30,163 --> 01:02:32,123
I didn't know
we lived in the same area.

813
01:02:33,083 --> 01:02:34,542
How come we haven't run
into each other until now?

814
01:02:42,300 --> 01:02:44,718
Bullying is the worst.

815
01:02:44,719 --> 01:02:46,471
Do you know how that feels?

816
01:02:48,807 --> 01:02:50,183
Maybe we have.

817
01:02:51,601 --> 01:02:52,602
At a neighborhood pub.

818
01:02:54,437 --> 01:02:55,438
What?

819
01:02:55,939 --> 01:02:57,232
If we ever have

820
01:02:58,400 --> 01:02:59,693
I bet it was
at a library or something.

821
01:03:00,235 --> 01:03:03,112
Because I don't go anywhere

822
01:03:03,113 --> 01:03:04,823
other than my house and the library.

823
01:03:05,657 --> 01:03:08,117
I didn't know we had a bar here.

824
01:03:08,118 --> 01:03:09,411
Why didn't I notice?

825
01:03:29,139 --> 01:03:30,807
What happened that night...

826
01:03:31,766 --> 01:03:33,810
Right. I might as well bury it.

827
01:03:35,395 --> 01:03:36,521
Mr. Kang.

828
01:03:37,022 --> 01:03:40,608
I'll keep your secret to my grave.

829
01:03:52,245 --> 01:03:54,705
That's my house right there.

830
01:03:54,706 --> 01:03:56,040
It's late. You should go home.

831
01:03:56,041 --> 01:03:57,417
But we're almost there.
Why would you...

832
01:03:57,751 --> 01:03:58,834
I'll walk you to your house.

833
01:03:58,835 --> 01:04:01,128
No, thank you for walking me home.

834
01:04:01,129 --> 01:04:03,840
You should go home. Thank you.

835
01:04:06,134 --> 01:04:07,468
It's slippery.

836
01:04:07,469 --> 01:04:08,928
- If you don't watch out...
- Mr. Kang!

837
01:04:50,929 --> 01:04:54,849
MY BIAS, MY BOSS

838
01:05:05,902 --> 01:05:08,530
EPILOGUE

839
01:06:18,349 --> 01:06:21,227
This is the last train
bound for Gudorim.

840
01:06:21,519 --> 01:06:26,232
Passengers for Songdam
must board this train.

841
01:06:27,025 --> 01:06:28,984
SUNGJU

842
01:06:28,985 --> 01:06:31,028
THIS TRAIN GUDORIM
NEXT TRAIN NONE

843
01:06:31,029 --> 01:06:32,906
GUDORIM

844
01:06:33,406 --> 01:06:35,074
INGUK STATION

845
01:06:43,541 --> 01:06:44,918
There's no chance she'd be here.

846
01:08:00,535 --> 01:08:01,536
What is this?

847
01:08:03,580 --> 01:08:04,747
Our stage!

848
01:08:05,373 --> 01:08:06,748
No!

849
01:08:06,749 --> 01:08:08,209
Let's cheer up just a bit more.

850
01:08:08,918 --> 01:08:10,211
- Is she pretty?
- Jeez.

851
01:08:10,920 --> 01:08:12,922
Was she too busy to call me?

852
01:08:13,965 --> 01:08:16,383
Unless our information is sent to SE
in real time

853
01:08:16,384 --> 01:08:17,968
- it's hard to find out.
- Taxi.

854
01:08:17,969 --> 01:08:19,053
Mr. Kang, you don't think

855
01:08:19,762 --> 01:08:20,930
the spy is...

856
01:08:21,472 --> 01:08:22,599
Ms. Nam.

857
01:08:23,808 --> 01:08:24,934
As of this moment

858
01:08:25,935 --> 01:08:27,020
you're fired.

859
01:08:42,076 --> 01:08:44,078
Subtitles by Eunsook Youn
and Songmi You
